WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.320
- This is an Electrobat.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.970
What's an Electrobat you ask?

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.200
Perhaps the love child of
Batman and a wall socket?

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.600
Or maybe a high-voltage vampire?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.140
Actually, no; but it is
something equally surprising.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.590
It turns out, New York City had

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:17.940
a fleet of electric taxis in 1895.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.361
Yes, 1895.

00:00:19.361 --> 00:00:22.361
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:25.920
(gentle music)

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.500
At the close of the 19th century,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.940
steam, gas and electric cars
were fighting for supremacy,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:32.950
but electric was leading the pack.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.630
Which is why a chemist named Pedro Salom

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.650
and an inventor named Henry Morris

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.870
built an electric vehicle called,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.533
yes, you guessed it, the Electrobat.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.280
Pedro and Henry took their creation

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.090
to the ultimate proving ground,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.190
the hectic streets of New York City,

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.810
where they ended up part of
the Electric Vehicle Company,

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.610
the first cab company of its
kind in New York and the world.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.140
The Electrobat was a hit.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.440
There were hundreds of them
zipping around Midtown.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.490
They had a battery station on Broadway.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:04.750
People loved them because you
didn't end up covered in soot.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:07.470
However, electric cars were almost twice

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.140
the price of their
combustion counterparts,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.860
and they had a limited range.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.990
So eventually the startup failed.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.590
At the dawn of the 20th century

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:18.030
taxis in New York City were green.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.320
But clean or no,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.570
the battery just didn't have
the juice to win the day.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.983
Perhaps they should've
tried out that vampire.

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:27.233
(laughing)

00:01:31.774 --> 00:01:35.107
(soft electronic music)

